### the excluded set S_E of eq:Sexc for the five curves y^2 = x^3 - D x
pari version      : [2, 17, 2]
field             : K = Q(i), d_K = -4
isogeny degrees [1,2] quoted from ../data/lmfdb_five_curves.json (2026-09-05);
supp(omega_E) empty (A = E, omega_E = 1), the paper's input to lem:comparison.

=== D = 56   E : y^2 = x^3 - 56x   LMFDB 12544.g1 ===
  conductor N       : 12544 = 2^8 * 7^2
  local c_q         : [[2, 2], [7, 2]]   product 4
  #E(Q)_tors        : 2
  isogeny_degrees   : [1, 2]   (quoted; a rational p-isogeny only at p = 2)
  Nm(f) = N/|d_K|   : 3136 = 2^6 * 7^2
  f                 : (1+i)^6 * (7)   generator f_0 = 56
  ideals of Z[i] of norm 3136 : 1   f is the conjugation-stable one
  Nm(f) - 1         : 3135 = 3 * 5 * 11 * 19
  S_bad             : {2, 3, 7}   from 6 N prod c_v #tors d_K = -2^14 * 3 * 7^2
  S_an              : {}   a_5 = -2, #Etilde(F_5) = 8   (5 is not anomalous)
  S_red             : {2}   from isogeny_degrees [1,2]: rhobar_{E,p} is irreducible at every odd p
  S_cmp             : {2, 3, 7}   from 6 N Nm(f) = 2^15 * 3 * 7^4   union the quoted supp(omega_E) = {2,7}
  S_cl              : {2, 3}   #Cl_f(K) = 384 = 2^7 * 3   structure [48, 4, 2]
  S_E               : {2, 3, 7}
  split primes in S_E                     : {}
  of those, of good reduction             : {}
  conj:EK guard #Cl_f(K) >= 6             : 1

